@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Terms of Service";
}
<!-- common banner -->
<section class="common-banner">
    <div class="common-banner__bg" style="background-image: url(images/banner/common-banner-03.jpg);"></div>
    <div class="common-banner__title">
        <h2>Terms of Service</h2>
        <a href="@Url.Action("Index", "Home")">home / </a>
        <span> Terms of Service</span>
    </div>
</section>
<!-- common banner -->
<!-- term of service -->
<section class="service">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="service-to-cotainer">
            <h2 class="title">NFT Marketplace Terms of Service</h2>
            <p>
                Welcome to our platform. These Terms of Service govern your access to and use of our website, including the purchase, sale, minting, and display of Non-Fungible Tokens (NFTs) through our services.
            </p>
            <p class="pt-4 pb-4">
                By accessing or using our platform, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agreed to be bound by these terms. If you do not agree to these terms, please immediately discontinue your use of <a href="@Url.Action("Index", "Home")">our website</a> and services.
            </p>
            <p class="pb-3">Please note that we provide a decentralized/custodial ecosystem for trading digital collectibles. We do not control the underlying blockchain networks, and all transactions executed are irreversible. Any interaction with NFTs on our platform is conducted entirely at your own risk.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="service-bottom-cotainer">
            <h6 class="title pb-3">1. Consent and Registration</h6>
            <div class="service-text-box">
                <p class="pb-4">By using our website, you hereby consent to our Privacy Policy and agree to its terms.</p>
                <p class="pb-2">1.1. To fully utilize our marketplace:</p>
                <p style="line-height: 35px;">
                    1.1.1. You must connect a compatible cryptocurrency wallet (e.g., MetaMask, WalletConnect). <br>
                    1.1.2. You are solely responsible for the security of your wallet, private keys, and all activities that occur under your connected wallet.
                </p>
                <p class="pt-1">
                    1.2. Trading NFTs involves significant financial risk. The value of digital assets is extremely volatile and can fluctuate drastically or drop to zero.
                </p>
                <p class="pb-4 pt-4">
                    1.3. The platform reserves the right to restrict access or block wallet addresses in the event of suspected fraud, copyright infringement, or money laundering.
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="service-bottom-cotainer">
            <h6 class="title pb-3">2. Intellectual Property and Ownership</h6>
            <div class="service-text-box">
                <p class="pb-4">Purchasing an NFT grants you ownership of the specific cryptographic token on the blockchain. However, it does not automatically transfer copyrights, intellectual property rights, or commercial reproduction rights of the underlying digital artwork, unless explicitly stated by the creator. You retain the right to resell, gift, and display your purchased NFT for personal use.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="service-bottom-cotainer">
            <h6 class="title pb-3">3. Fees and Payments (Service Fee & Gas)</h6>
            <div class="service-text-box">
                <p class="pb-4"><strong>3.1. Platform Service Fee:</strong> Our marketplace charges a fixed <strong>5% service fee</strong> on all successful transactions, including primary mints, secondary sales, and auction finalizations. This fee is automatically deducted from the final sale price at the moment the transaction is executed on the blockchain.</p>
                <p class="pb-4"><strong>3.2. Gas Fees:</strong> All transactions are also subject to network fees ("gas fees") determined by the underlying blockchain. Gas fees are paid directly to miners/validators and are completely non-refundable by our platform, even in the event of a failed or cancelled transaction.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="service-bottom-cotainer">
            <h6 class="title pb-3">4. Cookies and Web Beacons</h6>
            <div class="service-text-box">
                <p class="pb-4">Like any other website, our marketplace uses cookies. These cookies are used to store information including visitors' preferences, optimize the user interface, and track which pages on the website the visitor accessed or visited. This data allows us to enhance the user experience for both creators and collectors.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="service-bottom-cotainer">
            <h6 class="title pb-3">5. Children’s Information</h6>
            <div class="service-text-box">
                <p class="pb-4">This platform is intended solely for users who are 18 years of age or older (or the age of majority in your jurisdiction). We do not knowingly collect any personal identifiable information from children under this age. If you are under 18, executing transactions or creating an account on this platform is strictly prohibited.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
<!-- term of service -->